// FmaSgn -- the Pyrope equivalent of verilog/FmaSgn.sv (DatapathBench).
//
// Hand-written, not emitted from the Verilog: a machine emission would enter
// the same LGraph the Verilog does and measure the two FRONT ENDS rather than
// the two languages. See [status].pyrope in design.toml.
//
// Ports keep the Verilog names and the widths of the pinned point (BW = 12),
// so the generated harness and LEC bind the same external interface.
//
// a*b + c always fits the signed 24-bit result, so no `wrap`: the range
// check proves the Verilog never truncates here.
pub comb FmaSgn(a:s12, b:s12, c:s12) -> (res:s24) { res = (a*b) + c }
